{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>ללאת.</b> לצול\"ש בְּלַעַז, and so Onkelos renders עֲנוּבִין — a term of tying." "<b>At the edge of the set.</b> In that curtain at the end of the joining — the group of five curtains is called חוֹבֶרֶת." "<b>And likewise you shall do at the edge of the outermost curtain of the second set.</b> In that curtain which is קִיצוֹנָה — a term of edge, that is to say, at the end of the חוֹבֶרֶת."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The la'az לצול\"ש corresponds to Old French laz or los, 'loop'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:39.441085780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}